{"id": "wage-judgments-not-checked-at-bid", "title": "709 wage judgments on City contractors in five years; bidders’ records go unchecked", "seconds": 105.4, "voice": "elevenlabs:OtHu0lbpdNTqJVqaxDtR", "narrator": "Maven", "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "bc3ec68ad01e8eec", "words": 337, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["bl1", "story[0]"], "text": "December 2024. A supervisor had put a simple question to the Board’s analyst.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.7, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "bl1", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst · 2 December 2024", "text": "Considering Bidders’ Labor Law Violation History as part of City Procurement", "mark": "Labor Law Violation History"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.4, 0.64, 1.83, 1.97, 2.52, 2.62, 2.77, 2.83, 3.09, 3.48, 3.57, 3.67, 3.95]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "Does the City look at a bidder’s record of breaking labor laws before giving it a contract?", "t0": 4.82, "t1": 8.95, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "bl1", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst · 2 December 2024", "text": "Considering Bidders’ Labor Law Violation History as part of City Procurement", "mark": "Labor Law Violation History"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.28, 0.51, 0.71, 0.79, 0.85, 1.16, 1.48, 1.58, 1.94, 2.23, 2.51, 2.81, 3.04, 3.11, 3.18]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["story[0]", "suspicious[0]"], "text": "The answer, in the report’s first line: City departments do not screen bidders for it.", "t0": 8.95, "t1": 12.99, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "San Francisco City departments do not screen contract bidders for their history of compliance with federal, state, or local labor laws.", "kicker": "The report’s first line"}, "emph": ["do not screen"], "wt": [0.04, 0.22, 0.62, 0.72, 0.82, 1.17, 1.42, 2.08, 2.35, 2.81, 2.96, 3.14, 3.41, 3.71, 3.91]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "Six departments that buy construction and services were asked.", "t0": 13.21, "t1": 15.97, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Six departments asked", "kicker": "Construction and services", "sub": "Public Works, transportation, utilities, Public Health, homelessness, housing"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.8, 0.93, 1.18, 1.7, 1.81, 2.23, 2.38]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[1]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "They check that a bidder is registered and not debarred. They do not look back.", "t0": 16.09, "t1": 19.48, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "What is checked", "kicker": "Before an award", "sub": "registered, and not debarred"}, "emph": ["do not look back"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.37, 0.5, 0.56, 0.78, 0.88, 1.34, 1.45, 1.63, 2.42, 2.6, 2.73, 2.87, 3.04]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[0]"], "text": "And debarment is kept for “the most egregious” cases.", "t0": 19.6, "t1": 22.19, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "the most egregious", "kicker": "Debarment, per the City’s labor office"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.66, 0.79, 1.0, 1.12, 1.25, 1.5, 2.0]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "established[3]"], "text": "Yet construction bidders are already screened for their safety record.", "t0": 22.31, "t1": 25.36, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["safety record", "checked"], "b": ["labor-law record", "not checked"], "kicker": "Chapter 6 of the Administrative Code", "arrows": false}, "emph": ["safety record"], "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.78, 1.09, 1.25, 1.62, 2.02, 2.14, 2.3, 2.67]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "timeline[0]"], "text": "Meanwhile, the City’s own labor office was finding violations on City contracts. How many, in five years?", "t0": 25.58, "t1": 31.54, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Office of Labor Standards Enforcement", "kicker": "Fiscal 2018-19 to 2022-23", "sub": "closed cases with money judgments"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.52, 0.63, 0.92, 1.08, 1.39, 1.71, 1.83, 2.1, 2.67, 2.79, 3.02, 4.11, 4.3, 4.79, 4.96, 5.19]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "709 money judgments against City contractors.", "t0": 31.54, "t1": 34.28, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "709", "label": "judgments against City contractors, on their City contracts", "sub": "of 1,129 closed with judgments"}, "emph": ["709"], "wt": [0.04, 0.35, 0.64, 0.87, 1.11, 1.52, 1.76, 1.99]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "Most were for prevailing wage: 645 of them.", "t0": 34.8, "t1": 38.21, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "645 prevailing wage", "kicker": "Of the 709", "sub": "64 minimum compensation and health care accountability"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.35, 0.53, 0.69, 1.15, 1.93, 2.19, 2.5, 3.02, 3.15]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["amount"], "text": "And how much restitution was imposed on those contractors, for their workers?", "t0": 38.33, "t1": 42.09, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Office of Labor Standards Enforcement", "kicker": "Fiscal 2018-19 to 2022-23", "sub": "closed cases with money judgments"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.23, 0.42, 0.99, 1.11, 1.45, 1.53, 1.69, 2.36, 2.48, 2.72]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "suspicious[1].what"], "text": "18.5 million dollars, owed to the workers, not a City loss.", "t0": 42.09, "t1": 46.03, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$18,531,798", "label": "restitution imposed, owed to workers", "sub": "not a City loss"}, "emph": ["18.5 million"], "wt": [0.04, 0.42, 0.66, 0.93, 1.2, 2.06, 2.28, 2.39, 2.49, 3.04, 3.22, 3.28, 3.52]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "timeline[1]"], "text": "The cases rose from 117 a year to 160.", "t0": 46.45, "t1": 49.42, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["fiscal 2018-19", "117 cases"], "b": ["fiscal 2022-23", "160 cases"], "kicker": "Contract-law judgments a year", "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.43, 0.67, 0.86, 1.01, 1.27, 1.7, 1.78, 2.01, 2.14, 2.29, 2.52]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "story[1]"], "text": "These are the City’s own findings, yet no department interviewed reported looking them up.", "t0": 49.54, "t1": 53.51, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "This is not a practice reported by any departments we interviewed.", "kicker": "The analyst, on the labor office’s records"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.35, 0.49, 0.59, 0.92, 1.09, 1.74, 1.96, 2.11, 2.54, 2.96, 3.33, 3.59, 3.75]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "And those 709 judgments fell on how many firms?", "t0": 53.73, "t1": 56.9, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "709", "label": "judgments against City contractors, on their City contracts", "sub": "of 1,129 closed with judgments"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.38, 0.69, 0.96, 1.22, 1.67, 1.89, 2.02, 2.15, 2.35]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[1]"], "text": "572 contractors.", "t0": 56.9, "t1": 58.87, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "572", "label": "contractors, once repeat violators are removed", "sub": "709 judgments"}, "emph": ["572"], "wt": [0.04, 0.35, 0.63, 1.14]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "So some firms were found against more than once: 137 more judgments than firms.", "t0": 59.29, "t1": 64.24, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["judgments", "709"], "b": ["firms", "572"], "kicker": "137 more judgments than firms", "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.42, 0.74, 0.89, 1.12, 1.44, 1.59, 1.76, 2.56, 2.76, 3.04, 3.64, 3.85, 4.26, 4.43]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "Which firms, and whether they kept winning City work, the report does not say.", "t0": 64.36, "t1": 68.17, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["judgments", "709"], "b": ["firms", "572"], "kicker": "137 more judgments than firms", "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.75, 0.89, 1.12, 1.26, 1.51, 1.8, 2.08, 2.63, 2.79, 3.12, 3.28, 3.46]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why"], "text": "Repeat findings are what a bid check would be for.", "t0": 68.29, "t1": 70.32, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["judgments", "709"], "b": ["firms", "572"], "kicker": "137 more judgments than firms", "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.71, 0.8, 0.94, 1.01, 1.19, 1.41, 1.57, 1.72]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "State records were thinner: 5 of 150 contractors sampled had State wage judgments.", "t0": 70.44, "t1": 75.8, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "5 of 150", "kicker": "State Labor Commissioner records", "sub": "current City contractors sampled; name matches only"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.33, 0.62, 0.76, 1.6, 1.91, 2.07, 2.25, 2.51, 2.82, 3.41, 4.16, 4.35, 4.58, 4.81]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "The analyst warned that those matches were by name only.", "t0": 75.92, "t1": 78.62, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "5 of 150", "kicker": "State Labor Commissioner records", "sub": "current City contractors sampled; name matches only"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.5, 0.86, 1.02, 1.31, 1.68, 1.83, 2.0, 2.25]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["story[4]", "innocent[1]"], "text": "Department staff told the analyst many violations are clerical, corrected with restitution.", "t0": 78.84, "t1": 83.21, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "labor law violations are often due to clerical or administrative oversights by the violating company", "kicker": "Department staff, to the analyst"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.4, 0.66, 0.83, 0.95, 1.34, 1.61, 2.21, 2.33, 3.12, 3.53, 3.69]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["established[3]", "story[4]"], "text": "The analyst offered models: the safety-record check, or Los Angeles’s rule that bidders disclose past violations.", "t0": 83.33, "t1": 89.19, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "gavel", "name": "Safety-record check", "sub": "already applied to construction bidders"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Los Angeles", "sub": "bidders disclose past violations"}], "kicker": "The analyst’s models"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.47, 0.73, 1.56, 1.7, 2.41, 2.75, 2.92, 3.15, 3.65, 3.89, 4.02, 4.34, 4.8, 5.04]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "Not known: which firms, whether they won new work, and whether workers were paid.", "t0": 89.31, "t1": 92.97, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Which contractors the 709 judgments concern", "Whether a repeat violator won new City work", "Whether the restitution reached the workers"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.67, 0.92, 1.41, 1.71, 1.86, 2.06, 2.25, 2.55, 2.68, 2.93, 3.22, 3.36]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? The labor office’s case list, joined to later contracts by supplier number.", "t0": 93.09, "t1": 97.93, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "Office of Labor Standards Enforcement", "what": "Closed cases with judgments, by supplier number"}, {"who": "The Board", "what": "Whether it acted on the analyst’s options"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.29, 0.59, 1.0, 1.17, 1.45, 1.81, 2.12, 2.7, 3.03, 3.17, 3.45, 3.93, 4.07, 4.47]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "defense[0]"], "text": "The findings are the analyst’s; the report names no contractor and finds no wrongdoing.", "t0": 98.05, "t1": 102.24, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.52, 0.64, 0.76, 1.57, 1.73, 2.08, 2.36, 2.53, 3.1, 3.2, 3.48, 3.61]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 102.36, "t1": 104.5, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.65, 0.8, 1.06, 1.17, 1.26, 1.5, 1.76]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "lead1": "Nobody looks back", "lead2": "The City’s own records", "lead3": "More than once", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "flow", "hook": "number"}